== Abstract ==

This BIP defines the derivation scheme for HD wallets which create timelocked addresses used for creating fidelity bonds. It also gives advice to wallet developers on how to use fidelity bonds to sign over messages, such as certificates, which are needed when using fidelity bonds that are stored offline.

Two versions of the scheme are defined: v1, the original scheme already deployed in JoinMarket, and v2, a revision using a dedicated derivation <tt>purpose</tt> and a Miniscript-compatible <tt>witness script</tt>. Wallets SHOULD create new fidelity bonds using v2, and SHOULD also recognize v1 fidelity bonds that already exist.

